1
00:00:00,400 --> 00:00:04,212
Meet GeoWake: a destination alarm app built by a
solo

2
00:00:04,212 --> 00:00:07,775
developer, shown here in a controlled Android
demo.

3
00:00:08,400 --> 00:00:12,300
Choose a destination, then set when you would
like to be alerted

4
00:00:12,300 --> 00:00:12,500
.

5
00:00:12,500 --> 00:00:16,150
This example uses a metro stop threshold before
the journey

6
00:00:16,150 --> 00:00:16,975
starts.

7
00:00:20,350 --> 00:00:24,062
The app displays the route, estimated time
remaining, and

8
00:00:24,062 --> 00:00:26,038
distance to destination.

9
00:00:26,038 --> 00:00:29,750
Beside it, the developer dashboard feeds a
simulated journey into the

10
00:00:29,750 --> 00:00:30,600
demo.

11
00:00:36,375 --> 00:00:40,350
Speed and time controls make route scenarios
easier to inspect

12
00:00:40,350 --> 00:00:40,488
.

13
00:00:40,488 --> 00:00:43,838
This edit skips waiting time, while keeping the
setup,

14
00:00:43,838 --> 00:00:47,475
tracking, transfer notice, and arrival alert
visible.

15
00:00:52,375 --> 00:00:56,288
As the simulated journey approaches a transfer,
an Upcoming transfer

16
00:00:56,288 --> 00:01:00,188
notification appears, with controls to stop the
alarm or

17
00:01:00,188 --> 00:01:01,325
end tracking.

18
00:01:04,400 --> 00:01:08,112
Near the destination, a Wake Up notification
appears.

19
00:01:08,112 --> 00:01:10,837
The recording shows the visual alert state;

20
00:01:10,837 --> 00:01:14,725
its original audio track contains no audible
alarm.

21
00:01:17,375 --> 00:01:21,050
A second excerpt shows Map Tracking in dark
mode, with a road

22
00:01:21,050 --> 00:01:25,000
route and the same time, distance, and end-
tracking controls

23
00:01:25,000 --> 00:01:25,175
.

24
00:01:25,175 --> 00:01:27,900
These are recorded interface demonstrations.

25
00:01:34,400 --> 00:01:38,238
GeoWake 's archived codebase is offered for AI
training and

26
00:01:38,238 --> 00:01:39,650
evaluation.

27
00:01:39,650 --> 00:01:43,575
Its history includes route tracking, sensor
fusion experiments

28
00:01:43,575 --> 00:01:45,362
, and regression tests.

29
00:01:45,362 --> 00:01:49,312
Development stopped because collecting
underground calibration data

30
00:01:49,312 --> 00:01:51,050
became too costly.
